      "currency": "EUR",
      "description": "You paid one euro. This app knows it, and it won't let you forget it.\n\nTap the screen and get one sentence, big and bold, on a clean white screen. Sometimes it's a sarcastic one-liner about the purchase you just made. Sometimes it's a real quote about money, value and wanting things, from people who said it better than we ever could. Tap again for another.\n\nWHAT'S INSIDE\n- Nearly 600 lines, each one picked by hand\n- 300+ original sarcastic one-liners about money, impulse buys and the void\n- 250+ real quotes, each checked and attributed: Oscar Wilde, Mark Twain, Jane Austen, Benjamin Franklin, Warren Buffett, Seneca, Epictetus, Thoreau, Shakespeare, Terry Pratchett, Douglas Adams and more\n- Ambrose Bierce's Devil's Dictionary, stoic philosophy and famous one-liners from Dolly Parton to Winnie-the-Pooh\n- No repeats until you've seen every line\n- One tap per line, with nothing else on the screen\n\nWHAT'S NOT INSIDE\n- No ads\n- No subscriptions or in-app purchases\n- No accounts, no tracking, no data collection\n\nWHY PEOPLE BUY IT\n- A gag gift or prank for the friend who buys everything\n- To settle a bet that people will pay for anything\n- A daily dose of wit, wisdom and funny money quotes\n- Because minimalism deserves a sense of humor\n\n\"A cynic is a man who knows the price of everything and the value of nothing.\" — Oscar Wilde\nYou now know the price. The value is up to you.",
